> This behavior might have been introduced with the given_hparams 

@participant3 yes, it is because of that, which is a change needed for the `load_from_checkpoint` support from #18105 as mentioned in the bug description. Note that the issue only affects links applied on instantiate.

When I have the time I will work on a fix for this. I mentioned a workaround in my comment above.

@participant1 , thanks for the quick workaround. 
Can it be though that it this slows down the logging substantially? I am using the standard CSVLogger. After adding the workaround the training easily hangs for 20s in the steps when logs are written. Usually, I wouldn't even notice the logging. 
I struggle to see a direct connection.
